title: storage.transactions now genuinely implemented — mark (status implemented)
severity: low
status: triage
section: storage.transactions
reporter: agent (iteration 16, 2026-07-06)

summary:
  In iteration 16 the pgx transaction wrapper [Store.with_transaction]
  was added to image/lib/store.ml and used to wrap [fork_branch] (4 SQL
  statements) and [merge_branch] (1 INSERT ... ON CONFLICT). Both now
  run as a single SERIALIZABLE transaction per AGENTS.md and
  [storage.transactions] spec text. The spec doctrinal text is already
  correct ("SERIALIZABLE by default", "Postgres detects conflicts at
  commit and aborts one", "select-for-update exposed as a primitive"
  — note: select-for-update prim is NOT yet built; that's still
  TODO and should keep the status as `partial` or be split).

request:
  In the next borge plan pass, transition [storage.transactions] from
  (status planned) to (status implemented) — annotating that the
  SERIALIZABLE default with pgx with_transaction is wired through
  fork_branch and merge_branch. Do NOT mark `verified` until the
  - select-for-update prim is built and cross-checked, OR
  - split the subsection: a `with-transaction` subsection = implemented,
    a `select-for-update` subsection = planned.

  Reference agent note in pricklypear.borg should describe the actual
  implementation reality:
    - [Store.with_transaction ?isolation:Pg.Isolation.Serializable]
      lives in image/lib/store.ml (post-it16).
    - fork_branch: 4 SQL statements wrapped in with_transaction.
    - merge_branch: 1 statement wrapped (still atomic; tests cover this).
    - Variable: reads via recursive-CTE are NOT wrapped (they're read-
      only against the latest committed snapshot per connection —
      acceptable for read; SERIALIZABLE matters for mutations only).

verified-at-iteration:
  16 (2026-07-06)
  - dune build @all exit 0; dune runtest --force 92 tests pass.
  - Programmatic rollback verified: duplicate (fork 'main 'rbtest/child)
    raises on the branches(owner,name) UNIQUE constraint; pgx rolls back
    the partial INSERT, no orphaned branch row left behind (verified
    post-state: branches=1, function_defs=1).
  - Smoke tests green: pp_e2e_it6, pp_persist_it8, pp_route_it9,
    pp_checkout_it11, pp_fork_it9, pp_merge_it10, pp_crud_it13,
    pp_types_it14 — all re-tested under the transaction wrapper.

depends-on:
  BORGE-1783433175 (comprehensive plan-pass request — supersedes this
  for the bulk transition, but this issue adds storage.transactions
  specifically with the realized-with-transaction-flow context that
  BORGE-1783433175 didn't have at filing time).
